  "chapter": 650,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 41 Chapter 650\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 3204, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  establishing  the  400  Years  of African-American History\n        Commission; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon\n        expiration thereof\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill will establish the 400  Years  of  African-American  History\nCommission,  a  critical  and vital step towards fully understanding the\nmany contributions that African-American's have made to  the  growth  of\nNew  York  and the United States since the arrival of the first enslaved\nAfricans in Virginia in 1619. Moreover,  the  Commission  will  work  to\nbetter  appreciate, and acknowledge, the impact the harms of slavery and\nensuing racial discrimination have had on individuals of African descent\nliving in New York. Despite incredible, frequently  impossible  barriers\nAfrican-American's  perseverance and patriotism have continuously helped\nstrengthen New York and pushed the State to achieve its  fullest  poten-\ntial in ways which still have not been fully realized.\n \n  Unfortunately,  the current version of this legislation creates finan-\ncial and operational hurdles that were not accounted for in  its  draft-\ning.  The timelines for the Commission's work were ambitious, and it was\nunlikely that the State or the Commission could do this  critical  issue\njustice in such a short period of time.\n \n  Therefore,  I  have  reached an agreement with the legislature to make\nnecessary changes in order for the goals of this bill to be achieved. In\n1865, America outlawed slavery  forever,  but  the  ensuing  racism  and\nunequal  treatment  have  been issues New York has long fought to eradi-\ncate. While New York has made great strides in addressing many of  these\ninequities,  there is more work to be done. By signing this legislation,\nI am reaffirming New York State's commitment to continue  uplifting  the\ncontributions  of those in the African-American community, acknowledging\nthe unique hardships that its members have consistently fought to  over-\ncome,  and ensuring that New York continues to provide opportunities and\nsupport to the African-American community.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2019
 },
